/bigmac73nhs-log/172946","site":"T Nation · 457 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Squats and Milk-Journal from the Homeland of Hussars","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/squats-and-milk-journal-from-the-homeland-of-hussars/207551","site":"T Nation · 239 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Iraq War:  Any Alternatives?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/iraq-war-any-alternatives/42704","site":"T Nation · 121 posts · 2004"},{"title":"OMG Golden Corral","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/omg-golden-corral/159298","site":"T Nation · 94 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Future of Dentistry?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/future-of-dentistry/132212","site":"T Nation · 93 posts · 2009"},{"title":"To Experienced Fighters","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/to-experienced-fighters/74131","site":"T Nation · 66 posts · 2006"},{"title":"Dangers to Western Civilization","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/dangers-to-western-civilization/57817","site":"T Nation · 48 posts · 2006"},{"title":"Where Do You Find the Motivation?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/where-do-you-find-the-motivation/167990","site":"T Nation · 35 posts · 2011"},{"title":"wtf mouth widening device is legit","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/wtf-mouth-widening-device-is-legit.209571/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220406174237/https://looksmax.org/threads/wtf-mouth-widening-device-is-legit.209571/"},{"title":"wtf mouth widening is legit","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/wtf-mouth-widening-is-legit.203766/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220609195320/https://looksmax.org/threads/wtf-mouth-widening-is-legit.203766/"},{"title":"my results after 4 days of mouth widening before after","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/my-results-after-4-days-of-mouth-widening-before-after.167477/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230814174223/https://looksmax.org/threads/my-results-after-4-days-of-mouth-widening-before-after.167477/"},{"title":"does anyone know how to design 3d printed model of mouth widening device","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/does-anyone-know-how-to-design-3d-printed-model-of-mouth-widening-device.133062/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211119040331/https://looksmax.org/threads/does-anyone-know-how-to-design-3d-printed-model-of-mouth-widening-device.133062/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Microstomia - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microstomia"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Overall look","chain":["Appliance applies outward pressure at the mouth corners","Claimed gradual widening of the oral opening","Wider smile and different lower-face proportions"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Users wear a stretching appliance in the hope of making the mouth wider so the smile reads broader and better matched to the face. The effect is claimed in forum threads and has not been measured in published studies."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["A mouth widening appliance is a stretching device worn inside the mouth with the aim of widening the mouth and extending the corners of the smile. Looksmaxxing communities discuss mouth width as one proportion of the lower face and present the appliance as a non-surgical way to change it.[1][2]","The concept comes from clinical practice. Microstomia, an abnormally small mouth opening, can be congenital or follow burns or scleroderma, and clinicians manage it with surgery, prevention appliances, compression garments and therapist-guided exercise.[3] One forum thread asks whether a commercial 'adult microstomia prevention appliance' sold by a rehabilitation company is legitimate, and a reply describes it as 'pretty legit'.[4]","On looksmax.org, users share 3D models in sizes from 7 cm to 12 cm to be printed by a print shop, and the community has several guides, DIY designs and results threads.[2] No clinical studies have examined the devices for cosmetic widening."],"infobox":[["Type","Intraoral stretching appliance"],["Origin","Adapted from microstomia appliances"],["Forum variants","3D-printed (7-12 cm models), DIY, commercial clinical devices"],["Studies","No studies found for cosmetic use"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description and design","paras":["Appliances discussed in forums are rigid bars or frames sized to the target mouth width, placed between the corners of the lips.[2] Threads include DIY tool ideas and discussions of an alternative design intended to avoid smile lines.[5][6]","Models are shared as files for printing; one thread notes that someone without a printer can order the print from a service shop and that no account is needed beyond a free design site to export the file.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Medical background","paras":["Microstomia is treated clinically with intraoral appliances, manual stretching or exercises guided by speech or occupational therapists, and surgery to release scar tension. The literature stresses early, consistent intervention directed by a qualified clinician.[3]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in looksmaxxing","paras":["Members discuss mouth width as part of facial harmony and debate whether widening could help issues such as a long philtrum.[1] Other threads cover ordering appliances, 'results' posts and questions about downsides.[7][8]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found. Published literature on appliances concerns microstomia in patients, not cosmetic widening of a healthy mouth.[3]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Mouth widening is a recurring topic on looksmax.org, with guides, results threads and questions about whether the effect is real.[2][4]","claims":[{"claim":"Wearing a widening appliance can permanently widen the mouth","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Clinical microstomia appliances are the legitimate version of the approach","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Mouth widening for better philtrum?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mouth-widening-for-better-philtrum.527246/","source":"looksmax.o